      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "Nine people are killed in a mass shooting at a shack near Pretoria, South Africa.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "In 2003, Thabo Mbeki told parliament that the rural government militias, known as the Commando System, would be disbanded, despite warnings that this would leave rural areas vulnerable to a surge in crime.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385950565:142"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The crime rate later fell to 30 per 100,000 in 2011, then rose steadily to 44 per 100,000 in 2023, after a brief drop in 2020.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385950565:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:30Z",
      "text": "NBC News and AP reported the story.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:4",
        "wiki:2026-11-16:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:38Z",
      "text": "DW headlined its report, “South Africa: 17 killed in separate mass shooting incidents.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:dw:4668c90e6459"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:44Z",
      "text": "Sky News headlined its report, “At least 17 people killed in two separate shootings in South Africa.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:sky:18976cf851ad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:50Z",
      "text": "BBC News headlined its report, “Two mass shootings in South Africa leave 17 dead.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:bbc:f7febecbed77"
      ]
    },
